From 06459d1bae86e88432830e74399b707f1794b98d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 19:50:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 34/41] arm64: configs: drop dead
 CONFIG_INTERCONNECT_QCOM_MSM8998

This symbol does not exist on this tree -- there is no
drivers/interconnect/qcom/msm8998.c and no MSM8998 entry in
drivers/interconnect/qcom/Kconfig. olddefconfig was silently dropping
it, so the line was satisfied on paper and did nothing: exactly the
QFPROM-class trap the build runbook warns about.

Our 6.0 base does carry that driver; it was lost when this port moved
onto a v6.18 base pulled from GitHub instead of pristine kernel.org.
Leave the situation honest with a comment instead of a symbol that
reads as enabled but isn't. This is known debt blocking IPA/mobile
data, to be forward-ported later against the icc-rpm.{c,h} framework
using msm8996.c as the direct sibling template.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/taimen_defconfig | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/taimen_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/taimen_defconfig
index cc4a40d2d8fc..3ffd939978de 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/taimen_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/taimen_defconfig
@@ -4911,7 +4911,14 @@ CONFIG_INTERCONNECT_QCOM=y
 # CONFIG_INTERCONNECT_QCOM_MSM8939 is not set
 # CONFIG_INTERCONNECT_QCOM_MSM8974 is not set
 # CONFIG_INTERCONNECT_QCOM_MSM8996 is not set
-CONFIG_INTERCONNECT_QCOM_MSM8998=y
+# INTERCONNECT_QCOM_MSM8998 does not exist on this tree -- there is no driver
+# to select. Our 6.0 base has drivers/interconnect/qcom/msm8998.c; it was lost
+# when this port moved to the pristine v6.18 base and has not been
+# forward-ported. This is known debt that blocks IPA/mobile data. v6.18 has
+# the icc-rpm.{c,h} framework and msm8996.c as a direct sibling template for
+# the forward-port. Setting the symbol here was a silent no-op (the
+# QFPROM-class trap: olddefconfig drops unknown symbols without error) --
+# left removed rather than reintroduced as a lie.
 # CONFIG_INTERCONNECT_QCOM_OSM_L3 is not set
 # CONFIG_INTERCONNECT_QCOM_QCM2290 is not set
 # CONFIG_INTERCONNECT_QCOM_QCS404 is not set
-- 
2.55.0

